    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29118" root="عسل" body-key="E">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عِسْلُ مَالٍ</span></b>  (O, K) and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَالٍ</span> ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَسِيلُ</span></b>  (O) <i>i. q.</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِزَاؤُهُ</span>,
(O, K, TA,) i. e. <i>A good manager and pastor of
cattle,</i> or <i>camels &amp;c.:</i> the pl. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عِسْلٌ</span> is <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَعْسَالٌ</span>.
(TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هٰذَا عِسْلُ هٰذَا</span> means <i>This is the
like of this:</i> and so <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عِسْنُهُ</span>. (O.)

